Z||000000||TheFiero64||07-10-2000||04:55 PM||||He and myself have tried everything. I bled it 100% using Archie's method. I also replaced the slave and the master, and made sure it had the steel petal. <BR>I get the master to use its full stroke from top to bottom and the clutch still barly releases in the floorboards. It is impossible to drive. If you hold the clutch to the floor it disengages for 10 sec. or so then engages. I even put a spacer on the slave rod. Is there a way to get an oversized master or dose the second generation master have more volume. I think if I could just get the clutch fork in 1 more inch it would be fine. I Give up on the F*** Thing.<BR>I don't know how he drives it. It is close to driving without pushing a clutch at all. <B>HELP</B><P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Patrick||07-10-2000||05:41 PM||||<BR>I'd be curious what the diameter is of the slave cylinder you're using. Below is something I had posted in an older thread.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>This may or may not help. Go to this infamous mega-thread on clutches and read it over.<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000034-3.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000034-3.html</A> <P>To help narrow things down, maybe you can start with my post from <B>09-18-1999 04:13 AM</B> and read down to and include <B>09-19-1999 04:13 PM</B>. See if that's of any help.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hope you find something of interest.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||07-11-2000||12:07 AM||||THIS IS A QUOTE FROM ARCHISMS:<P>"ONE FINAL NOTE: Some people have the same alum. pedal symptoms but have a steel pedal. I have seen one case where the steel pedal<BR>had a similar problem and when replaced with a new steel pedal the problem was cured".<P>Does this mean that a steel pedal &lt;may&gt; be bent??????<P>You said you needed 1 more inch. When I replaced my pedal the old aluminum one didn't look like it was bent??? but the new steel pedal cured the prob.So from what I understand it doesn't take much of a bend to cause you this prob.<BR>It's worth a try!!<P>DXR_DAD<P> <p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 07-11-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000003||Patrick||07-14-2000||02:22 AM||||<BR>Joshua, the least you could do is to acknowledge that a couple of forum members tried to help you out. Maybe our suggestions were of no help, but never-the-less, we took the time to offer our assistance. <P>This forum is based on people volunteering their time and knowledge. Lack of gratitude by enough people would eventually destroy the whole format. <P>Possibly this was just a rare oversight on your part...||||reg||8
Z||000004||TheFiero64||07-14-2000||04:37 PM||||I'm <B>sorry</B>. I have had a bad couple of days. I haven't even had the time to sit for 2 sec. As some of you may know I work for UPS on the Graveyard shift. Most of my Management team has just been transferred and I Have been working around the clock to teach the new crew. I have also been helping my mother who just had hand surgery. In-fact I just got in from Bringing her to Boston and back because the pin was popping out of her hand. I have been up for 20+ hours. So I am <B>very sorry</B> if I hurt your feelings, I always try to reply and <B>THANK</B> everyone that helps me. I think the <B>Pennock's Family</B> is a special thing and I agree with you 100%. I also have hurt feelings that you just jumped the gun and posted this message in a public forum. You could have at least e-mailed me in private before making me out as the bad Guy. I hope there are no hard feelings.<P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000005||TheFiero64||07-14-2000||04:48 PM||||Thanks for the help Patrick & DXR_DAD. I think I am going to put the 2nd design master cylinder in. I have been led to believe that it gives a little more volume. I like the Idea of using ATF instead of dot 3, but I'm not sure because I have also heard that it destroys the seals. Any long term users? I may also try a suggestion I got that involves  installing a little valve inline that holds 5 or 10 lb.. of fluid in the slave when you release the clutch. This may however cause the t.o. bearing to wear. I don't want to have to take the cradle out if I can help it. I will try a few experiments and post my progress when I do them.<P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick||07-15-2000||02:37 AM||||<BR>Joshua, before this gets turned around to make <I>ME</I> look like "bad guy", let me just say a few things. First, I checked the forum before I last posted in this thread and I found that you had made numerous posts elsewhere since DXR_DAD and I offered our suggestions. So you weren't quite "working around the clock" all that time. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Secondly, I think I more than gave you the benefit of the doubt with the last sentence in my previous post, as it was honestly stated without any malice or sarcasm. Thirdly, posting what I did in this forum instead of privately emailing you serves to remind others here who are NOT as conscientious as you to remember how this forum works.<P>My sympathies are with you regarding your mother's health and well-being. I just spent 10 hours in the emergency ward on Tuesday watching my 80 year old mother writhing and crying in agony with some kind of abdominal problem which still hasn't been diagnosed. With that and then me going to the hospital everyday since, yeah, it's been a lousy last few days for me also. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>Anyway, I certainly don't have any hard feelings. You had the class to respond to my last post. I respect that. Onto your clutch problems...<P>I don't know myself whether or not there is any difference in the volume of fluid displaced by the "2nd design" master cylinder. As you're probably aware, the more fluid displaced by a larger master cylinder (within reason), the better. Conversely, the smaller the diameter (within reason) of the slave cylinder, the better, because this will allow the slave piston (and thus the clutch) travel to be greater. This is why I was interested in the diameter of your slave cylinder, because it has been established beyond any doubt that there are two different sizes- 13/16 and 15/16 inches. You want a 13/16 inch slave.<P>I have had ATF in my clutch hydraulic system since late last August, so that's about eleven months at this point. My clutch has continued to work like new since I made the conversion. It disengages perfectly now, and I never have to bleed it any more. If you read that mega-thread on clutches that I provided the link for, you'll know the problems I had before I made the switch. However...<P><B>DO NOT USE <I>ATF</I> WITH NEW MASTER AND/OR SLAVE CYLINDERS!!!</B><P>There have been numerous problems when people used ATF with new cylinders. The seals have a tendency to swell up so much that the pistons get jammed in the bores. As a last resort, only try using ATF with older components.<P>The in-line valve idea sounds like trouble waiting to happen. You don't want to prevent the slave from returning to its rest position. The idea is to get the slave to move as far as possible (within reason) when you step on the clutch pedal. If it's moving far enough (just under an inch) and the clutch is not disengaging properly, the problem is unfortunately elsewhere.<P>Good luck, keep us posted.||||reg||14
Z||000007||TheFiero64||07-15-2000||03:12 PM||||OK thanks Patrick, I will keep you posted. I hope to see him this week. I don't get to see him as we both work and he lives 1/2 hour away. I worked on it yesterday but didn't get to the clutch. I did the swaybar endlinks. They were very bad. I wonder how to find out the diameter of the slave?<P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000008||Patrick||07-16-2000||03:49 PM||||<BR>I had measured the diameter of my slave when it was out of the car and disassembled. (Even then I mistakenly thought it was 3/4 inch.) However...<P>If you simply pop the pushrod out from between the slave and the clutch release lever while the slave is still installed, you should be able to measure the bore size of the slave. The dust cover (boot) may be clamped to the pushrod, but that's fine, just remove it at the same time as the rod. It's got to come off anyway to be able to see the bore at the end of the slave.<P>My 13/16 inch slave has a smooth outer appearance, much like the master cylinder. At one time when I was trying to replace the slave, I was supplied with a slave that had a rough, cast iron appearing finish. It turned out to have a 15/16 inch bore, so I took it back and have continued to use the original slave (with ATF). The 15/16 inch slave supposedly was the correct Raybestos unit according to their catalog for my ‘87 2.5L 5-speed (Isuzu), but it was definitely the wrong one. The parts guy scornfully insisted I had the wrong transmission in the car. Idiot... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||TheFiero64||07-16-2000||06:06 PM||||Ok, Next time he comes by. I will measure it. Thanks.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000010||Mattsfiero||07-19-2000||03:09 PM||||Okay I want to start by saying thankyou to everyone who has offered suggestions. I Personaly plan on checking the Diameter of the Slave cyclinder and making sure I am using the 13/16 that Patrick mentioned I will also be switching to the new designed Master wich appears to Have a longer throw. seeing the old style has the Fluid reserve in the front and the piping out back(Closer to the fire wall and the new style as everyone knows has the piping out front and the reserve in the back.<P><BR>By the way The fiero64 Is my brother in so to speak terms....(Have known him for 17 years) and I thank him Impateheticaly for all the help and for posting this message. <P>Again thank you everyone<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smile08.gif"> <BR>Matt <BR>||||reg||1
